# PayPal sandbox credentials for the Curator demo (Act 3).
# NEVER put real credentials in the repo — copy this file to server/.env
# (or repo-root .env) and fill it in locally.
#
# How to get sandbox credentials, free, no card needed:
#   1. Go to https://developer.paypal.com/ and log in (or create a free
#      PayPal developer account).
#   2. Open Apps & Credentials: https://developer.paypal.com/dashboard/applications
#   3. Make sure the Sandbox toggle is on (NOT Live), click "Create App",
#      give it a name (e.g. paypal-curator-demo).
#   4. Copy the Client ID and the Secret (click "Show") into the lines below.
#
# Which account's app? The sandbox order's money settles to the merchant
# account that owns these credentials — so for the demo ("agent pays
# contractor M. Okafor"), use the contractor's sandbox business account's
# app, or a sandbox business account standing in for them. See
# server/README.md for the full two-account demo setup.
#
# Payer approval: a sandbox order must be approved by a sandbox BUYER
# (personal) account before it can be captured. Create one at
# https://developer.paypal.com/dashboard/accounts (Sandbox > Accounts >
# Create Account > Personal), fund it with fake money, and log in with it
# when you open the approve link the API returns.
PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID=
PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET=

# SANDBOX only. The server refuses to start paying if this is PRODUCTION
# (or anything else). Leave it exactly as it is.
PAYPAL_ENVIRONMENT=SANDBOX

# Server port.
PORT=3000

# Optional: how long to wait for the PayPal sandbox to answer before the
# server gives up honestly (milliseconds). The toolkit sets no HTTP
# timeout of its own, so this guard stops a hung PayPal call from hanging
# the demo. Default 30000.
# PAYPAL_TIMEOUT_MS=30000

# Optional: URLs the sandbox buyer returns to / cancels to after approving
# in the PayPal web flow. If unset, the toolkit defaults to example.com.
# PAYPAL_RETURN_URL=
# PAYPAL_CANCEL_URL=
